        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/c7d62336-415d-4ae3-80be-65e025187d75,1770996336103/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C2560%2C1440%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='A man holds up a necklace.' width='620' height='349' title='Jeff Probst holds up a Hidden Immunity Idol during Tribal Council during the 28th season of Survivor.'/><p>Survivor airs its 50th season Feb. 25, marking 25 years of one of the longest-running reality TV shows. And experts say its premiere \u2014 and the seasons that followed \u2014 changed the landscape of reality television.</p>",
