        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/bb86fded-9f57-47e2-bccb-5c0787b13b11,1771619211895/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C104%2C2000%2C1125%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='A man and a woman sit in a vehicle, with the woman holding a young child.' width='620' height='349' title='Mustafa Alio and Muzna Dureid, along with their young son, boarded a small bus to reach Dureid\u2019s aunt\u2019s neighbourhood \u2014 the only way into the area, which was inaccessible by car due to war damage and rubble \u2014 in December 2024.'/><p>It's been a little over a year since the fall of Bashar al-Assad in Syria ended a 14-year civil war. More than 1.3 million Syrians have returned home since then, according to the UN refugee agency, primarily from neighbouring countries such as Turkey, Lebanon, Jordan, Iraq and Egypt \u2014 but also from as far away as Canada.</p>",
